# The journal records what the player saw and did, and a visit goes on the chronicler's queue when it ends.
#
# A meet_stranger conversation with the brewer is the shortest route through all four kinds of entry:
# narration (the opening observation, the thinking, the outcome), dialogue (the brewer's lines and the
# one reply picked, never the options left), a fact (the outcome's chip) and milestones (the first visit,
# a modus mentis learned). Leaving for the world map then closes the visit's group: it is queued for the
# chronicler, and until it is written the journal shows it raw.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal meet_stranger
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

wait mode Dialogue 60
advance 20 180
click option 0
advance 20 180
click option 0
advance 20 180
click continue
advance 20 180
expect Courteous, and you know when to stop
click button
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# --- the journal, mid-visit -----------------------------------------------------------
manage Journal
wait 1
expect J O U R N A L
expect ◆ DAY 1
expect First came to the
expect ✦ Learned
expect Good day
expect Courteous, and you know when to stop
expect-not not yet written up
expect-state journal pending-groups=0
dump

# --- the visit ends: queued, still shown raw ------------------------------------------
manage
click button
wait mode WorldView 60
manage Journal
wait 1
expect 1 visit not yet written up
expect Good day
expect-state journal pending-groups=1
expect-state journal kind=Dialogue state=Pending
expect-state journal kind=Milestone
save roundtrip
quit
